    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nThis is an extension of #376.\r\n> When it comes to doing surround operations count1 should apply to the operator and count2 should apply to the object.\r\n\r\nThis should apply to deletion and replacement operations too, making `2sd(` convert `(foo (b*r)) baz` to `foo bar baz` in place of `foo (bar) baz` which would instead be achieved via `sd2(`.\r\nSimilarly, `2sr)]` would turn `(foo (b*r)) baz` into `[foo [bar]] baz`, and `sr2)]` would result in `[foo (bar)] baz`.\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2024-01-31T10:49:56Z",
